Article 3
(1) The objectives of the protection of Children and Women from acts of violence are: a. to prevent and eliminate all forms of acts of violence and exploitation against children and women that occur in the family environment and society;
b. to pursue recovery and social reintegration for children and women victims of acts of violence;
c. to provide services to children and women victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. to carry out empowerment for women victims of violence; and e. to increase community participation.
(2) The implementation of protection of children and women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), includes aspects of:
a. prevention;
b. services and assistance;
c. social reintegration; and
d. empowerment.

REGENT OF BANTUL,

Considering : a. that every child and woman has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain a sense of security, free from all forms of violence, discrimination and violations of the rights of women and children;
b. that acts of violence against children and women continue to increase, so that comprehensive and maximum protection efforts are needed, concrete actions, formal institutional support, regulations that can guarantee implementation from the Regional Government in increasing broad community participation;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within the Special Region of Jogjakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
7. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
8. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
9. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
10. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning the Determination of the Effective Date of Laws of 1950 Numbers 12, 13, 14 and 15 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 59);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 Concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
18. Regional Regulation of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Number 3 of 2012 concerning the Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Year 2012 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Number 3);
19.Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 7 of 2005 concerning Transparency and Public Participation in the Implementation of Government in Bantul Regency (Regional Gazette of Bantul Regency Year 2005 Series C Number 1);
20.Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 13 of 2007 concerning the Determination of Mandatory and Optional Government Affairs of Bantul Regency (Regional Gazette of Bantul Regency Year 2007 Series D Number 11);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANTUL REGENCY, and

